WEBVTT

00:15.310 --> 00:20.150
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

00:20.360 --> 00:25.610
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

00:25.820 --> 00:30.700
Prayers won't solve anything

00:30.910 --> 00:36.040
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

00:36.250 --> 00:41.340
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

00:41.540 --> 00:43.880
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

00:44.090 --> 00:46.760
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

00:46.970 --> 00:52.140
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

00:52.350 --> 00:57.440
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

00:57.640 --> 01:02.650
consumed with surging bloodlust,

01:02.860 --> 01:09.780
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

01:31.988 --> 01:36.993
The World the Girl Saw: The Struggle for Trost, Part 2

01:37.350 --> 01:38.680
Hey!

01:38.890 --> 01:40.520
Hey! What's wrong, Armin?!

01:40.730 --> 01:41.690
Pull yourself together!

01:41.900 --> 01:42.810
Hey!

01:43.020 --> 01:45.360
Armin! Hey, Armin!

01:45.570 --> 01:46.980
Hey!

01:47.740 --> 01:50.200
You with me?! You okay?!

01:50.400 --> 01:53.370
Are you all right? Where's your squad?

01:53.570 --> 01:55.080
Squad...?

01:55.280 --> 01:56.950
Oh, man. Pull yourself together.

01:57.160 --> 01:58.830
Why are you all by yourself?

01:59.040 --> 02:01.830
Plus you're all wet and slimy...

02:02.040 --> 02:04.170
What the hell happened?

02:09.550 --> 02:12.260
You're so useless! Just die already!

02:12.470 --> 02:14.550
- Whoa! Calm down, Armin!
- Damn it!

02:14.760 --> 02:16.600
Where is everyone?!

02:17.100 --> 02:19.140
Give it a rest, Conny.

02:19.350 --> 02:22.310
They've been wiped out. All but him.

02:22.520 --> 02:25.110
Shut up! Armin hasn't said anything!

02:25.310 --> 02:27.150
Just look around. It's obvious.

02:27.360 --> 02:30.320
We don't got any
more time to waste on him.

02:30.530 --> 02:32.570
Why is he the only one who's okay?!

02:32.780 --> 02:36.240
Beats me. Maybe they
thought he was a corpse?

02:36.450 --> 02:39.540
It sucks that they
ran into multiple Titans

02:39.750 --> 02:41.960
and that only this
underachiever made it out alive.

02:42.160 --> 02:44.120
Eren and the others
worked hard for nothing.

02:44.330 --> 02:46.340
You bitch...

02:46.540 --> 02:48.800
Want me to make it
so you never talk again?!

02:49.000 --> 02:50.380
Stop it, you two!

02:50.590 --> 02:53.010
We're all shaken up here!

02:53.220 --> 02:55.890
All our friends are suddenly
dying left and right!

02:56.100 --> 02:57.350
It's natural we're upset!

02:57.560 --> 03:03.100
That's my Christa!
Marry me when this is over!

03:03.310 --> 03:04.730
Yeah...

03:05.270 --> 03:07.730
She is clowning
around more than usual.

03:08.480 --> 03:10.320
Anyways, we can't stay here.

03:10.530 --> 03:12.570
Can you stand, Armin?!

03:16.240 --> 03:19.030
I'm sorry for the trouble.

03:20.040 --> 03:22.040
I'll rendezvous with the rearguard.

03:22.250 --> 03:22.960
Hey...

03:23.160 --> 03:24.580
Armin!

03:28.210 --> 03:32.050
Let's go, Conny!
We've been ordered to advance!

03:36.470 --> 03:38.350
This is hell...

03:38.550 --> 03:42.770
No, it hasn't become hell.

03:42.980 --> 03:46.270
I was just mistaken until now.

03:46.480 --> 03:50.610
This world has always been hell,
from the very start.

03:52.480 --> 03:55.610
The strong prey on the weak.

03:55.820 --> 03:58.990
It's such a simple,
straightforward world.

04:00.030 --> 04:03.000
It's just, my friends...

04:05.830 --> 04:10.130
They tried to be strong in this world.

04:11.630 --> 04:15.550
They helped me, someone who was weak.

04:15.760 --> 04:19.140
I couldn't bear it...

04:19.350 --> 04:23.680
They saw me as someone
who needed to be protected.

04:23.890 --> 04:26.060
I wanted to live
in this world like them...

04:26.270 --> 04:32.400
I wanted to be strong and stand
shoulder-to-shoulder with them...

04:40.700 --> 04:43.290
And this is the result.

04:43.490 --> 04:46.410
Because of me, Eren wound up...

04:58.260 --> 04:59.390
Hanna...

04:59.590 --> 05:01.640
What are you doing?

05:01.850 --> 05:02.930
Armin! Help!

05:03.140 --> 05:05.600
Franz isn't breathing!

05:05.810 --> 05:11.360
I've tried resuscitating him
over and over and over...

05:12.060 --> 05:13.900
...but it's not working!

05:14.110 --> 05:16.400
It's dangerous down here, Hanna.

05:16.610 --> 05:20.490
- You need to get on a roof...
- I can't just leave Franz like this!

05:20.700 --> 05:23.740
You don't understand, Hanna...

05:23.950 --> 05:25.580
Franz is...

05:32.750 --> 05:36.760
Please... stop this...

05:37.510 --> 05:38.720
I...

05:40.840 --> 05:44.100
I can't take this anymore...

05:44.300 --> 05:46.020
I can't...

05:51.310 --> 05:56.150
H-Hey, now! Don't you guys
realize how bad the situation is?!

05:56.360 --> 05:58.820
Yeah! That's why we're doin' this!

05:59.030 --> 06:01.280
And if you guys wanna live,
you'll give us some damn help!

06:01.490 --> 06:03.280
- The hell with that!
- It's gonna get stuck!

06:03.490 --> 06:06.490
- Letting people through comes first!
- We're all gonna get eaten standing here!

06:06.700 --> 06:09.960
- What are you doing, soldier?!
- Go get 'em!

06:10.160 --> 06:11.540
B-But...

06:11.750 --> 06:16.130
Just try it, small fry! I'm the boss
of this town's merchant association!

06:16.340 --> 06:18.260
Uhh, err...

06:18.460 --> 06:22.590
Who do you think pays for
the meals you soldiers shit out?!

06:22.800 --> 06:26.260
Do you have the money to
provide for the soldiers in this town?!

06:26.470 --> 06:27.930
Push, all of you!

06:28.140 --> 06:33.190
This cargo's worth more than you
can earn in your entire measly lives!

06:33.400 --> 06:35.810
Help, and you'll be rewarded!

06:36.020 --> 06:37.360
It'll be okay.

06:37.570 --> 06:41.700
Your dad's going to use his
cannons to make the Titans go away.

06:41.900 --> 06:43.610
Mom.

06:43.820 --> 06:45.450
Over there.

06:56.170 --> 06:57.380
Push!

06:57.590 --> 06:59.460
Push if you don't wanna die!

06:59.670 --> 07:01.300
Stop! The children...!

07:06.220 --> 07:08.720
Damn! Why is it ignoring us?!

07:08.930 --> 07:11.390
It's an Abnormal!
No point trying to figure it out!

07:11.600 --> 07:14.810
It's fast! Not even we
elites can catch up to it!

07:15.020 --> 07:16.860
At this rate...!

07:36.830 --> 07:39.460
What... are you doing?

07:39.670 --> 07:41.550
Oh, perfect timing!

07:41.760 --> 07:44.380
Get these guys to help me!

07:44.590 --> 07:47.010
I'll make it worth your while!

07:48.890 --> 07:52.680
My comrades are dying as we speak.

07:52.890 --> 07:58.560
They're fighting and dying because
the citizens haven't finished evacuating.

07:58.770 --> 08:00.070
Of course they are!

08:00.270 --> 08:02.400
It's your duty to give your hearts

08:02.610 --> 08:05.450
to defend the lives
and property of the people!

08:05.650 --> 08:08.370
Don't go gettin' a big head now
that you freeloaders have somethin' to do

08:08.570 --> 08:10.410
after a century of uselessness!

08:19.080 --> 08:22.750
If you feel people dying for
other people is a matter of course,

08:22.960 --> 08:28.550
then I'm sure you'll understand
that a single, precious life

08:28.760 --> 08:31.180
can sometimes save
the lives of many as well.

08:31.390 --> 08:32.810
Just you try it!

08:33.020 --> 08:35.520
Your employer and I go way back!

08:35.730 --> 08:40.730
One word from me and
he'll be all over your sorry ass!

08:44.480 --> 08:46.490
How can a dead body talk?

08:49.320 --> 08:50.740
Wait!

08:54.540 --> 08:57.210
S-Sir!

08:57.410 --> 08:59.250
Pull the cart out.

09:08.180 --> 09:10.390
Thanks, lady!

09:10.590 --> 09:14.770
You really saved the day.
You have our gratitude!

09:40.370 --> 09:43.630
Good work taking it down,
Ackermann. Very impressive.

09:43.840 --> 09:47.010
Thank you, Sir. However...

09:47.210 --> 09:51.510
I'm afraid I inadvertently dulled
my blades during the attack.

09:51.720 --> 09:53.930
I will be more careful next time.

09:54.930 --> 09:58.350
Just what have
you had to live through...?

09:58.560 --> 10:00.560
No, never mind.

10:06.480 --> 10:09.990
Why am I reminded
of it at a time like this?

10:28.510 --> 10:30.130
Finished!

10:30.340 --> 10:31.880
Look, Mom!

10:32.090 --> 10:34.930
Oh, you did a great job, Mikasa!

10:35.140 --> 10:36.970
It's very nice!

10:38.020 --> 10:40.230
This style of embroidery has
been passed down in our clan

10:40.430 --> 10:42.770
from generation to generation.

10:42.980 --> 10:46.320
When you have a child,
it'll be your turn to pass it on too!

10:47.570 --> 10:49.440
How can I have a child?

10:49.650 --> 10:53.110
Err, why don't you ask your father that?

10:53.320 --> 10:54.610
Well, Dad?

10:54.820 --> 10:57.780
Oh, uhh, I don't really know, either!

10:57.990 --> 11:00.700
Oh, I know!
Dr. Jaeger will be here any minute!

11:00.910 --> 11:03.250
Why don't we ask him?

11:05.880 --> 11:08.840
Oh, that must be him!

11:11.380 --> 11:12.800
Coming!

11:18.180 --> 11:18.970
Mikasa?

11:19.180 --> 11:22.810
Yes. She's about your age.

11:23.020 --> 11:27.150
There aren't many children
in these parts, so try to get along.

11:27.360 --> 11:29.860
That depends on how she acts...

11:30.070 --> 11:31.360
Eren.

11:31.570 --> 11:34.860
That attitude is why
you've only made one friend.

11:36.370 --> 11:37.950
Are they not home?

11:39.030 --> 11:40.120
Mr. Ackermann!

11:40.330 --> 11:42.160
It's Jaeger!

11:44.500 --> 11:46.330
Is anyone home?

11:48.630 --> 11:50.130
What's wrong?

11:51.590 --> 11:53.550
What is it, Dad?

12:02.020 --> 12:03.310
Too late.

12:03.520 --> 12:04.600
Eren.

12:04.810 --> 12:09.110
Have you seen the girl..
Mikasa... anywhere nearby?

12:09.310 --> 12:10.650
No.

12:10.860 --> 12:12.280
I see...

12:13.490 --> 12:16.660
I'll get the Military Police
and have them conduct a search!

12:16.860 --> 12:18.700
You'll wait at the foot of the mountain.

12:18.910 --> 12:21.410
Is that clear, Eren?!

12:22.540 --> 12:23.950
Eren!

12:30.460 --> 12:34.880
Hey. Are you sure she'll actually sell?

12:35.090 --> 12:38.010
We even went and killed her
parents before running off with her...

12:38.220 --> 12:41.140
Take a look at her face.

12:42.720 --> 12:47.060
Looks nice, but she's
still just a kid. She ain't for me.

12:47.270 --> 12:49.860
I'm not asking about your tastes.

12:50.060 --> 12:52.110
She's an "Oriental."

12:52.320 --> 12:55.490
There used to be different types
of humans, you see.

12:55.690 --> 12:58.030
Long ago, some people
fled a place called the Orient

12:58.240 --> 13:00.030
and sought refuge inside the walls.

13:00.240 --> 13:02.780
She's the last descendant of that clan.

13:02.990 --> 13:05.540
We're gonna take her to the
underground market in the capital

13:05.750 --> 13:08.540
and auction her off to those old perverts.

13:08.750 --> 13:12.880
All the other Orientals have died out,
so she'll go for a pretty hefty price.

13:13.090 --> 13:16.420
Her old man didn't
look like an Oriental to me.

13:16.630 --> 13:18.380
She ain't pureblooded.

13:19.590 --> 13:22.760
That's right! The mom
was the really valuable one!

13:22.970 --> 13:24.600
But you had to freak out and kill her!

13:24.810 --> 13:27.640
I-I couldn't help it! She put up a fight!

13:27.850 --> 13:30.600
That all you got
to say for yourself?! Huh?!

13:36.110 --> 13:36.990
Dr. Jaeger!

13:37.190 --> 13:39.030
We've been expecting...

13:51.830 --> 13:53.840
Hello. Pardon the intrusion.

13:59.930 --> 14:01.840
Just take it nice and easy,

14:02.050 --> 14:05.430
unless you want
your head split open with this.

14:07.520 --> 14:08.730
This broad's crazy!

14:08.930 --> 14:10.440
Mikasa! Run!

14:10.640 --> 14:12.100
Huh? M-Mom...

14:12.310 --> 14:14.230
Hurry, Mikasa!

14:15.150 --> 14:17.150
Uhh...

14:17.360 --> 14:18.400
Dad...?

14:18.610 --> 14:21.700
Damn it! I've had enough of your crap!

14:34.460 --> 14:37.420
What the hell?!
I said only kill the dad!

14:37.630 --> 14:39.800
Don't look at me!
She's the one who...!

14:40.010 --> 14:42.220
Save your excuses! Go get the kid!

14:42.430 --> 14:43.840
Huh?!

14:46.560 --> 14:47.390
Hey.

14:47.600 --> 14:49.890
You better behave yourself.

14:51.180 --> 14:53.980
Or else... this!

15:05.030 --> 15:06.450
Cold...

15:17.460 --> 15:19.460
Excuse me...

15:20.300 --> 15:21.720
Hold it, kid!

15:21.920 --> 15:24.050
How did you find this place?!

15:24.260 --> 15:25.840
Err, uhh...

15:26.050 --> 15:31.310
I got lost in the forest,
and then, umm, I saw a cabin, so...

15:36.020 --> 15:40.570
You know kids shouldn't
wander around the forest all alone.

15:40.780 --> 15:44.320
Scary wolves live
in the forest, you know.

15:44.530 --> 15:46.950
But there's nothing to
worry about now.

15:47.160 --> 15:49.660
We'll be happy to take you...

15:51.370 --> 15:53.460
Thanks, Mister.

15:53.660 --> 15:55.960
I already know the score.

15:56.920 --> 15:59.920
So die, you asshole!

16:02.090 --> 16:05.840
Huh?! What the hell?!

16:06.050 --> 16:09.100
G-Get back here, kid!

16:15.230 --> 16:17.600
You damn animal...!

16:17.810 --> 16:20.110
Die! Die!

16:20.320 --> 16:24.900
This is what you get!
This is what you deserve!

16:25.110 --> 16:28.490
Never get up again!

16:43.340 --> 16:47.840
You're safe now...
You can relax.

16:50.640 --> 16:53.060
I take it you're Mikasa?

16:53.260 --> 16:54.560
I'm Eren.

16:54.770 --> 16:59.900
I'm Dr. Jaeger's son.
I'm sure you've met my dad before.

17:00.110 --> 17:03.270
I was tagging along when he
visited your house for a checkup.

17:03.480 --> 17:05.110
But then...

17:07.740 --> 17:09.950
There were three of them.

17:19.960 --> 17:21.580
Was it you?

17:24.800 --> 17:26.170
Was it you who killed 'em?!

17:26.380 --> 17:27.970
Was it?!

17:28.170 --> 17:31.890
I'm gonna kill you!
I'm gonna kill you!

17:32.100 --> 17:34.810
F-Fight!

17:35.010 --> 17:36.850
Fight!

17:37.060 --> 17:40.650
Fight... or die...!

17:40.850 --> 17:43.060
Win... and live!

17:43.270 --> 17:46.280
What the hell are you thinking, brat?!

17:46.480 --> 17:50.030
The only way to win...
is to fight!

17:55.540 --> 17:57.830
No... I can't do it!

18:06.550 --> 18:10.430
Just then... I remembered.

18:10.630 --> 18:13.300
I had seen this same thing...

18:13.510 --> 18:16.430
...over and over...

18:16.640 --> 18:18.520
...all my life.

18:20.390 --> 18:24.400
I'd seen it everywhere I went...

18:24.610 --> 18:26.020
But...

18:26.860 --> 18:29.570
I always looked the other way.

18:32.030 --> 18:33.450
"That's right...

18:35.370 --> 18:36.990
We live...

18:38.830 --> 18:40.830
...in a cruel world."

18:49.090 --> 18:53.380
At that moment,
my body stopped shaking.

18:53.590 --> 18:58.520
I was in full control of
myself after that.

19:00.060 --> 19:02.770
I thought I could do anything...

19:02.980 --> 19:04.400
"Fight."

19:09.190 --> 19:10.610
"Fight!"

19:11.490 --> 19:12.900
"Fight!"

19:23.500 --> 19:26.710
Stabbed through the heart from behind.

19:26.920 --> 19:29.630
Those kids did this?

19:34.680 --> 19:38.300
Eren. I told you to wait
at the foot of the mountain.

19:38.510 --> 19:41.770
Do you have any idea what you've done?!

19:41.980 --> 19:44.270
I got rid of some dangerous animals!

19:44.480 --> 19:47.230
They just happened to look like people!

19:47.440 --> 19:48.690
Eren!

19:48.900 --> 19:52.940
They would've been long gone
by the time the Military Police arrived!

19:53.150 --> 19:54.570
It would've been too late!

19:54.780 --> 19:59.530
Even so, you were just lucky, Eren!

19:59.740 --> 20:04.870
The way you casually threw
your life away is what I'm angry about!

20:05.080 --> 20:06.960
But...

20:07.170 --> 20:10.380
I wanted to save her as fast as I could...

20:14.090 --> 20:17.550
Mikasa. Do you remember me?

20:17.760 --> 20:21.180
We've met several times before,
when you were little.

20:23.640 --> 20:25.730
Dr. Jaeger...

20:25.940 --> 20:31.150
How do I get home from here?

20:32.780 --> 20:35.110
I'm cold...

20:35.320 --> 20:40.120
I have nowhere to go now...

20:50.790 --> 20:52.800
You can keep this.

20:56.260 --> 20:58.340
Warm, isn't it?

21:04.180 --> 21:06.640
It is...

21:06.850 --> 21:07.980
Mikasa.

21:08.190 --> 21:10.310
Come live with us.

21:10.520 --> 21:12.070
Huh?

21:12.270 --> 21:15.440
You've been through a lot.

21:15.650 --> 21:19.110
You need plenty of rest.

21:21.200 --> 21:22.740
What is it?

21:22.950 --> 21:26.200
C'mon. Let's go already.

21:26.410 --> 21:28.370
To our home.

21:32.590 --> 21:34.420
Yeah. Let's go...

21:49.440 --> 21:54.270
A cruel world in which only
the victors are allowed to live...

21:58.950 --> 22:00.110
Time to withdraw, Ackermann!

22:00.320 --> 22:01.660
Let's scale the wall!

22:01.860 --> 22:03.910
I'll go assist the vanguard's retreat!

22:04.120 --> 22:06.200
H-Hey, Ackermann!

22:06.410 --> 22:11.000
But I do have a place to
call home in this world now.

22:12.960 --> 22:14.210
Eren.

22:14.420 --> 22:18.420
As long as I have you,
I can do anything.

22:36.480 --> 22:41.400
Your dreams are where your heart is

22:41.610 --> 22:47.660
They're more fragile than life itself

22:47.870 --> 22:52.330
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

22:52.540 --> 22:59.010
Now, rest in peace

22:59.210 --> 23:10.350
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

23:10.560 --> 23:20.610
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

23:20.820 --> 23:26.570
In this beautiful, cruel world

23:26.780 --> 23:31.750
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

23:31.950 --> 23:37.460
Oh, with our strength... and our weakness...

23:37.670 --> 23:43.130
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

23:43.340 --> 23:46.760
to anything anymore?

23:53.940 --> 23:57.480
"I have a place to call home."

23:57.690 --> 24:01.940
After finishing her rearguard duties,
Mikasa hurries to see Eren,

24:02.150 --> 24:05.133
only to learn of his death.

24:05.133 --> 24:06.160
Small Blade: The Struggle for Trost, Part 3
only to learn of his death.

24:06.160 --> 24:07.010
Small Blade: The Struggle for Trost, Part 3
